(footprint "TI_DN023_IFA__868___915_MHz" (version 20221018) (generator pcb_antenna_designer)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "Meandered inverted-F antenna from TI design note DN023 (SWRA228, CC1110EM), dimensions from its Table 1: 43 x 20 mm above a 45 x 31 mm ground plane, 0.8 mm FR-4, no ground under the antenna. Here L6 = 15 and L2 = 3 put it on 868 MHz (TI: L6 = 11 measured through a 15 mm feed line with matching pads). The antenna is electrically small (20 mm tall at 868 MHz), so its resistance is low, about 15 - j15 ohm: it needs a matching network, as in TI's board. In the Matching tab, series 6.8 nH then shunt 5.6 pF (Wurth 0402) give about -33 dB, -10 dB from 862 to 874 MHz. L6 tunes the frequency: shorter for 915 MHz. Parameter names as in the note.")
  (tags "antenna IFA MIFA RF")
